140|- Root LOGBOOK patch (`.temp/resume-20260916/logbook-preserved-07.patch`) and\n141|  stash record (`logbook-stash-08.txt`) intact; no root LOGBOOK write was\n142|  made — findings live in this artifact per the brief.\n143|\n144|## Checklist truth table\n145|\n146|1. Exact prospective composition: CHECKED — published tree `b383baa...`\n147|   byte-equals the independently reviewed prospective tree; only accepted\n148|   mapper/test bytes composed; prior signed ancestry and fixture diagnostics\n149|   preserved.\n150|2. Signed commit by Ivan Oparin: CHECKED — single explicit `-S` commit with\n151|   current timestamps; verified locally and on GitHub after publication.\n152|3. Hosted CI observed honestly: CHECKED — real exact-head run 35087910852\n153|   observed to completion (`failure`); complete outcome + job identities +\n154|   full log attached; wifiAware resolution distinguished from the newly\n155|   exposed `weak let` failure; no green claim, no landing, no repair, no\n156|   unchanged-condition retry, no VPN operation.\n157|4. Code per task description/AC: CHECKED — publication-only scope honored;\n158|   no new product code authored.\n159|5. Outcome artifact: CHECKED — this file plus the attached CI log, both\n160|   task-scoped `TASK-260916-235lb7_*` outcomes.\n161|6. Logbook: CHECKED — no new root LOGBOOK write per the brief (evidence\n162|   attached here instead); preserved patch/stash verified intact.\n163|\n164|## Handoff state and recommendation\n165|\n166|- Ready for review (handed off to review). PR6 (`310a560`) awaits independent\n167|  exact-head review and owns its green-checks/landing obligations under\n168|  TASK-260908-34gi0y; nothing was landed here.\n169|- The `M1RuntimeCommand.swift:138` `weak let` defect needs a fresh scoped\n170|  repair route (new BUG with its own diagnosis/review/green cycle), mirroring\n171|  how the wifiAware defect was routed. It is new product work outside this\n172|  publication task and was deliberately not to