{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9a9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9f3-0aae-7543-b404-eee867114d41"},"sequence":815,"recorded_at":1780531400001625,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a55aec8e-a7e3-4a93-bd48-0c1f165c8ec5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a55aec8e-a7e3-4a93-bd48-0c1f165c8ec5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a55aec8e-a7e3-4a93-bd48-0c1f165c8ec5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a9f6-782d-71e3-bead-06529d247a99"},"task_id":"01a0a9f6-782d-71e3-bead-06529d247a99","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a9f6-782d-71e3-bead-06529d247a99","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1_results.md`.\n1|# BUG-260916-2764p8 results: weak-capture compilation repair\n2|\n3|## Diagnosis\n4|Hosted run35087910852 failed at Sources/ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport/M1RuntimeCommand.swift:138:16 with `weak must be a mutable variable`.\n5|Root cause: line 138 declared `weak let weakHostOwner = hostOwner`. Older Swift (hosted macos-15 CI toolchain) rejects `weak let`\n6|as a language-level error; `weak` references must be `var` because ARC zeroes them at runtime. The declaration feeds the\n7|release check at lines 169-173 (`hostOwner = nil; guard weakHostOwner == nil else { throw hostLifetimeInvariant }`).\n8|Only occurrence of `weak let` in Sources/ and Tests/ (regex search) — no sibling sites.\n9|\n10|## Fix (1 line, semantics-preserving)\n11|```diff\n12|-      weak let weakHostOwner = hostOwner\n13|+      weak var weakHostOwner = hostOwner\n14|```\n15|File: Sources/ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport/M1RuntimeCommand.swift:138. No behavior change: same ARC-zeroed weak optional,\n16|same nil-check, same hostLifetimeInvariant gate, same cancellation/ownership flow. No new tests: brief directs reuse of\n17|existing M1 ownership/release suites; a compiler-spelling fix has no new behavior to cover.\n18|\n19|## Prerequisite stack identity (reused bytes, NOT new scope)\n20|- PR6 head: 310a560916d8b8012fa238f65b51649041caee4d (verified via rev-parse; also origin/delivery/STORY-260715-1y04r0-rev3)\n21|- Worktree HEAD (unmoved): b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74 on task-board/story/STORY-260916-1du4i1, nothing committed\n22|- Overlay: all tracked non-board paths checked out from PR6 head; staged diff stat exactly matches\n23|  `git diff b3422b0..310a560` (59 files, 8970 insertions, 65 deletions)\n24|- Pre-fix file blob == PR6 blob: bcd896110682117e347fda955c9024e71297e9cf (exact identity)\n25|- Post-fix file blob: d868eb7be3849c8aa0da84a0423de6c5476ebb38\n26|- New delta vs PR6 head (`git diff 310a560 --stat`): 1 file, 1 insertion, 1 deletion (the line above)\n27|- Candidate layout: staged = prerequisite overlay; unstaged = new delta only; .task-board artifact untouched; no untracked files\n28|\n29|## Validation (all on full composed candidate, real code, exit codes observed)\n30|- `swift build --target ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport` (pre-fix, PR6 bytes): exit 0 — local Swift 6.3.2 ACCEPTS `weak let`,\n31|  so the hosted failure is NOT reproducible on this toolchain (see bound below). Minimal swiftc -typecheck probe confirms.\n32|- `swift build --target ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport` (post-fix): exit 0, one benign warning:\n33|  `#WeakMutability: weak variable was never mutated; consider let` — new-toolchain-only diagnostic; no warnings-as-errors\n34|  in Package.swift; `weak var` is the unique spelling compiling on both old (hosted) and new (local) Swift.\n35|- `swift build` (all targets): exit 0\n36|- `swift test --filter M1RuntimeHarnessTests|DeterministicSessionFactory`: 9 tests, 2 suites, pass, exit 0\n37|- `swift test --filter MacOSProductionRuntimeOwnership|M1RuntimeComposition`: 11 tests, 2 suites, pass, exit 0\n38|- Combined post-restore re-run: 20 tests, 4 suites, pass, exit 0\n39|- Real binary end-to-end: `swift build --product ReluxTunnelHarness` exit 0, then\n40|  `python3 scripts/validate-m1-runtime-harness.py --executable .build/debug/ReluxTunnelHarness`: passed=True, 7/7 fixtures, exit 0\n41|  (validator asserts zero `harness.m1.host_owner_retained` gauge through the fixed production path)\n42|- Narrowing mutant (weak->strong `var weakHostOwner`, gate stays present): `swift test --filter M1RuntimeHarnessTests`\n43|  FAILS, 6 tests, 14 issues, exit 1 (hostLifetimeInvariant fires, exit .failure) — proves the suite guards weak semantics;\n44|  mutant reverted, green re-observed after restore (20/20 above)\n45|- Lint: no linter configured in repo (no lint target in Makefile/CI); only diagnostic is the known benign #WeakMutability warning\n46|\n47|## AC coverage: 4 of 4 rows driven through production entry\n48|Production call site: HarnessApplication.run([m1-runtime,...]) -> M1RuntimeHarnessCommand.run (M1RuntimeCommand.swift:118).\n49|1. Weak-reference semantics correct: productionEntryDoesNotRetainOrConsultHostOwner + successfulComposedGenerations\n50|   assert exit .success and host_owner_retained==0 through the production entry; mutant proves sensitivity.\n51|2. Runtime ownership correct: macOS production runtime ownership suite + M1 runtime composition suite (11 tests) pass.\n52|3. Focused validation passes + toolchain bounds recorded: this document; see bound below.\n53|4. Prerequisite identities + new delta independently reviewable: identities and 1-line diff above; candidate uncommitted.\n54|\n55|## Toolchain / proof bounds (honest)\n56|- Local: Apple Swift 6.3.2 (swiftlang-6.3.2.1.108 clang-2100.1.1.101), Xcode 26.5 (17F42), macOS 27.0 host,\n57|  target arm64-apple-macosx28.0. Per toolchain-bound note, NO compiler version is asserted for hosted run35087910852\n58|  (macos-15, unpinned, log has no version strings).\n59|- Local toolchain accepts BOTH spellings, so this run proves the repair compiles and behaves correctly on Swift 6.3.2\n60|  but cannot reproduce the original hosted error; hosted proof on the older toolchain remains a subsequent delivery gate\n61|  (accepted per task AC, not a producer handoff prerequisite).\n62|- Full credential-free/xcodebuild gate not run locally (requires legacy relux-proxy root + generated workspace); SwiftPM\n63|  build/test + real-binary fixture validation is the focused bound.\n64|\n65|## Prospective composition boundary\n66|Uncommitted candidate = exact PR6 prerequisite bytes (staged, 59 files) + 1-line weak-var delta (unstaged).\n67|Independent review: verify staged tree equals PR6 head minus .task-board, then review the single unstaged hunk.\n68|No publication, branch commit, VPN operation, routing change, or unrelated fix performed.","final_result":true}}}
